{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>I will serve you seven years.</b> These are 'a few days' — as his mother said to him: ״וְיָשַׁבְתָּ עִמּוֹ יָמִים אֲחָדִים״ (Genesis Rabbah). And know that this is so, for it is written: ״וַיִּהְיוּ בְעֵינָיו כְּיָמִים אֲחָדִים״ (Genesis 29)." "<b>For Rachel your younger daughter.</b> All these signs — why? Because he knows him to be a deceiver, he said to him: I will serve you for Rachel — but perhaps you will say, a different Rachel from the marketplace; therefore it says ״your daughter.״ And perhaps you will say, I will swap Leah's name and call her name Rachel; therefore it says ״the younger.״ And even so it did not help, for he deceived him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:07.848862967Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}